WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.410
A king falls on a stage.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.720
Then the stage folds flat into a book.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.570
Inside, a young woman
walks a long country road.

4
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.800
Turn the page: a man on a
lawn gazes at a green light,

5
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.340
in a novel from 1925.

6
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:21.000
Its last line: "So we beat
on, boats against the current,

7
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.020
borne back ceaselessly into the past."

8
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.380
No stage, no actors, no chorus.

9
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.400
So can a novel, or even
a poem, be a tragedy?

10
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.700
In this mission, you'll ask whether
a tragedy needs a king at its centre.

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.180
And you'll test Hardy and Keats
against the oldest rules of tragedy.

12
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.680
Your mission: decide whether
tragedy can survive off the stage.
